// Gnome Flinger

@0 = ~Wooden Catapult~
@1 = ~Gnome Flinger~

@10 = ~Catapults are siege engines that use leverage and gravity to hurl heavy projectiles over great distances.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 15~
@11 = ~Among the more questionable achievements of the planar tinker gnomes of Krynn, few have achieved the notoriety of the Gnome Flinger. It was ostensibly designed as a means of transporting small creatures across dangerous gaps.

The basic principle is deceptively simple: a gnome is placed within a padded launching craddle. A series of gears and tensioned springs are engaged, and the machine hurls its occupant through the air. A properly calibrated Gnome Flinger can send a willing gnome a remarkable distance. The planar tinker gnomes claim the invention was inspired by the natural resilience of their people and the inability to resist pressing a lever marked "DO NOT PRESS."

Several years ago, a particularly ambitious group of tinker gnomes departed Krynn aboard a spelljammer vessel and traveled through the Astral reaches. They eventually arrived in Sigil, the City of Doors. There, surrounded by portals, fiends, modrons, adventurers, and creatures from a hundred worlds, the gnomes believed they had finally discovered the ideal marketplace for their inventions. They established a workshop and began demonstrating their various contraptions to the city's residents, including the Gnome Flinger. Despite the initial reluctance of Sigil's inhabitants to try out the gnomes' contraptions, there was enough demand to keep the workshop going.

This particular Gnome Flinger has already seen much use. The launching craddle is designed to carry members of any of the short races. However, only the gnomes' innate resilience allows them to use the device without the danger of getting hurt on impact.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Fling creature
  Range: 40 ft.
  Area of Effect: The user
  Using the device takes a full round.
  Only members of the short races (e.g. gnomes, halflings, or dwarves) can use the device.
  Halflings and Dwarves must save vs. Wand or take 1d8 non-lethal damage on impact.

Requires:
 6 Strength

Weight: 15~

@20 = ~Flinger is being prepared...~
@21 = ~Unable to use the flinger~
